# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Factory credentials — copy to .env.factory and fill in.
#
# These are ORG-LEVEL tokens the factory authenticates with in order to CREATE a
# product's resources. They are not product secrets and must never be copied into an
# app's .env — product credentials live in Infisical and are materialised into
# apps/<product>/{api,mobile}/.env.
#
# Anything set in the real environment wins over this file, so CI can inject tokens
# without one on disk.
#
# A driver whose credentials are missing is skipped with a clear message and blocks
# only its dependents — you can start with a few and add the rest later.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GitHub — repo creation + Actions secrets. Needs `repo` and `admin:org` scopes.
GITHUB_TOKEN=""

# Infisical — machine identity with Universal Auth (Organization Settings →
# Access Control → Identities). The identity must be able to create projects.
INFISICAL_CLIENT_ID=""
INFISICAL_CLIENT_SECRET=""
INFISICAL_ORG_ID=""

# Neon — a personal or organization API key (Account settings → API keys). It must
# be able to create projects; each product+environment gets its own.
NEON_API_KEY=""

# Sent.dm (SMS/WhatsApp/RCS) — an API key from Settings → API Keys. Optional: with
# it the factory creates the product's delivery webhook and captures its signing
# secret; without it, `factory apply` emits a manual step instead of failing.
SENT_DM_API_KEY=""

# Vercel — account or team token. Set VERCEL_TEAM_ID when the projects live in a team.
VERCEL_TOKEN=""
VERCEL_TEAM_ID=""

# Sentry — org auth token with project:write and project:read.
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=""

# PostHog — personal API key with organization + project write scopes.
# POSTHOG_ORG_ID defaults to "@current" when omitted.
POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=""
POSTHOG_ORG_ID=""

# Resend — a full-access API key. Used to create per-product sending keys.
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# Cloudflare — API token scoped to Zone:DNS:Edit on the zones you provision into.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""

# Expo — a robot access token (expo.dev → Account settings → Access tokens).
EXPO_TOKEN=""

# Clerk — a Platform API key (beta). With it, the factory creates one Clerk
# application per product and pulls that instance's keys. Without it, Clerk falls
# back to a manual step; everything else still provisions.
# Requires the `clerk` CLI on PATH: pnpm add -g clerk
CLERK_PLATFORM_API_KEY=""

# Stripe — the shared account's secret key. Products, prices and webhook endpoints
# are created inside it and separated by metadata. Creating a separate ACCOUNT per
# product needs a reviewed Stripe App (Claimable Sandboxes) — see the stripe driver.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""

# Anthropic — OPTIONAL admin key, used only to pre-create a Workspace per product.
# API keys themselves cannot be created via API; that stays a manual step.
ANTHROPIC_ADMIN_KEY=""
